KZ3 patch 2208 (rsx): [o0-lpb], the LightProbe 8x8 block probe (RSX_O0=1; off by default; probe only, no behaviour change).
Per flip: the 8x8 W16Z16Y16X16F location-1 texture binds (the blocks SPU job 9 writes into the ring 1:0x0005C180-0x00C8F700), distinct offsets,
new texture-cache entries (recycled = an evicted resource reused), per-bind content hashes, hashes that changed, in-place redecodes vs replaced
resources, bytes bound, bytes uploaded (new + changed blocks), and the 4 KiB pages of the new/changed blocks as copy spans (contiguous, and merged
across gaps of up to 16 pages). Per bind: the VP hash and FP location:offset:size (and pipeline key) current for the draw (the pipeline is built before
the texture loop) and the unit's sampler filter, so "bound with other than point sampling" is a counter (nonpoint, [o0-lpb-use] nonpoint=, [o0-lpb-filt]).
Output (stderr, walker thread, no locks): `[o0-lpb] flip=N binds= distinct= new= recycled= hashed= changed= inplace= replaced= boundKB= decKB= dpages= dspans=
dspans16= nonpoint= users=` for the first RSX_O0_LPB_N (default 30) flips that had a block bind; every RSX_O0_LPB_WIN (default 60) flips a
`[o0-lpb] win flips= active= <field>=avg/max ...` line with run totals, then `[o0-lpb-use] vp= fp= pso= binds= nonpoint=` per consumer and `[o0-lpb-filt]
min= mag= mips= aniso= point= binds=` per sampler state (cumulative over the run). Off: one predicted-not-taken test of g_rsx_lpb.on per texture bind.
libs/video/rsx_lpb.h is pure C (host test tools/smoke/test_lpb.sh). ASSUMPTIONS: dirty pages count only blocks the walker hashed as changed or created
(the clean rules skip some hashes, so it is a lower bound of a page bitmap); 4 KiB pages; point = min NEAREST/NEAREST_NEAREST and mag NEAREST (the
conservative reading: a mip-linear min filter on a one-level block counts as not point). Not run in the game (no GPU this round).

